 "verdict": "the_fold_removes_N_accesses_and_none_of_them_names_the_counted_key_of_its_own_row_so_it_hides_no_read;_but_K_of_the_locations_E636_reports_as_reading_the_counted_key_below_the_receiver_are_the_same_locations_where_E633_counts_a_recognised_read,_so_the_two_instruments_draw_the_boundary_at_different_depths_and_neither_lost_a_read",
 "answer": "E633 folds 9 access(es) out of the same-key census across 7 of its 13 counted read line(s) (depths 2 x3, 3 x6).  3 of them name a literal key (cutoff, eq_s) and 6 name none; 0 name the counted key of their own row.  5 of those line(s) also sit in E636's population, and on 4 of them E636 reports the counted key itself as read below the receiver -- 4 of which E633 simultaneously counts as a recognised read of that key on the same line, 0 of which E633 counts nothing at all."
